## 1. Hydraulic stack, CDU to plate (18 LPM per 15 kW package; reference rack = 18 trays x 1 package = 324 LPM, 270 kW; 4 racks ~ 1.08 MW)
tray loop (single UQD08): Rev A 42-51 kPa vs CoolIT-like 56-79 kPa; dual UQD08: Rev A ~17-20 kPa
rack + CDU 80 kPa: loop head Rev A 122-131 vs 136-159 kPa -> saving 11-18 %
rack + CDU 124 kPa: loop head Rev A 166-175 vs 180-203 kPa -> saving 8-14 %
rack + CDU 180 kPa: loop head Rev A 222-231 vs 236-259 kPa -> saving 6-11 %
head-limited CDU (assumed 250 kPa available, 100 kPa CDU+piping at reference flow, 20 kPa rack manifold+hoses): Rev A N/Nref = 1.356
head-limited CDU (assumed 250 kPa available, 100 kPa CDU+piping at reference flow, 20 kPa rack manifold+hoses): CoolIT-like N/Nref = 1.275
-> racks per head-limited CDU: +6 % for homogeneous Rev A racks (assumption-driven)
pump power saved per plate 4.3 W hydraulic, 8.6 W electrical at 50 % wire-to-water; per 100 MW: 58 kW -> US$40k/yr at US$0.08/kWh
CDU capex credit when head-limited (research base US$9-25 per plate): US$60-167k per 100 MW, one-time
mixed racks: Rev A branches need 20-50 kPa keyed orifices (verify-hydraulics rack.py): system saving = 0
start-up 17 C: Rev A plate dP at 18 LPM ~9.4 kPa (inertial 6.05 + viscous 1.55 x mu ratio); CoolIT-like ~41 kPa (16 kPa viscous assumed)
start-up 25 C: Rev A plate dP at 18 LPM ~8.7 kPa (inertial 6.05 + viscous 1.55 x mu ratio); CoolIT-like ~33 kPa (16 kPa viscous assumed)
start-up 45 C: Rev A plate dP at 18 LPM ~7.6 kPa (inertial 6.05 + viscous 1.55 x mu ratio); CoolIT-like ~22 kPa (16 kPa viscous assumed)

## 2. Return temperature and heat reuse (15 kW, max-case limit 85 C, return cap 65 C)
0.75 LPM/kW (rise 20.3 K): return CoolIT paste 61.1 / PCM 65.0 C; Rev A paste 65.0 / PCM 65.0 C (thermal limit, P50)
1.0 LPM/kW (rise 15.2 K): return CoolIT paste 56.0 / PCM 59.9 C; Rev A paste 61.5 / PCM 65.0 C (thermal limit, P50)
1.2 LPM/kW (rise 12.7 K): return CoolIT paste 53.5 / PCM 57.4 C; Rev A paste 59.0 / PCM 62.9 C (thermal limit, P50)
CoolIT PCM 1.2 LPM/kW: return 57.2 C -> heat-pump COP to 80 C ~6.2
Rev A PCM 1.2 LPM/kW: return 62.7 C -> heat-pump COP to 80 C ~7.6
20 MW reused (ERF 20 % of 100 MW): heat-pump electricity 3.9 vs 3.0 MW -> 0.8 MW less; at 6,000 h/yr and US$0.10/kWh: US$0.51 M/yr (contingent on loop-wide supply temperature)
hot-dry (Phoenix-class): adiabatic hours at 45 C supply ~800, at +5.5 K ~200 (illustrative climate assumption) -> ~600 h removed; water at 0.4-0.8 L/kWh-rejected x 100 MW: 24-48 thousand m3/yr
temperate (Frankfurt-class): adiabatic hours at 45 C supply ~5, at +5.5 K ~0 (illustrative climate assumption) -> ~5 h removed; water at 0.4-0.8 L/kWh-rejected x 100 MW: 0-0 thousand m3/yr
hot-humid (Singapore-class): adiabatic hours at 45 C supply ~0, at +5.5 K ~0 (illustrative climate assumption) -> ~0 h removed; water at 0.4-0.8 L/kWh-rejected x 100 MW: 0-0 thousand m3/yr
Rev A PKG-A (vacuum braze, BAg): cradle-to-gate ~8.6 kgCO2e (Cu 1.43 kg buy, Ag 5.0 g; screening factors, ISO 14067 study needed)
Rev A C2 (Cu-Sn TLP): cradle-to-gate ~7.6 kgCO2e (Cu 1.43 kg buy, Ag 0.0 g; screening factors, ISO 14067 study needed)
incumbent like-sized (est.): cradle-to-gate ~10.7 kgCO2e (Cu 2.0 kg buy, Ag 2.5 g; screening factors, ISO 14067 study needed)
pump-energy saving 76 kWh/yr per plate -> 30 kgCO2e/yr at 0.4 kg/kWh (homogeneous racks only)

